From 2d826fb0ddffe1137dce1aeed130ade836329f62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:59:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 232/233] debug: raise the trace depth guard to 3000 for long
 method chains

Every call in a method chain nests one level deeper in the HIR, and the
expression visitors open a TRACE_FUNCTION frame per visit, three per call
in typecheck's ExprVisitor_Apply. skim 5.7.3 options.rs:

    #[derive(derive_more::Debug)]
    pub struct SkimOptions { /* 153 fields, 4 #[debug(skip)] */ }
        // -> __f.debug_struct("SkimOptions").field("..", &self.a) x149 .finish()

    Typecheck Expressions
    Assertion failed: (g_debug_indent_level<MAX_INDENT_LEVEL), function TraceLog, file src/debug.cpp

The 450 limit (raised for curl-sys's build script chain) lets about 145
calls through. A builtin derive(Debug) on a struct that size builds the
same chain.

The counter only guards against runaway recursion: real stack use is about
2KiB per call in a chain (x86-64, -O0: 63K at 20 calls, 307K at 140, under
2M at 950), so 3000 (~1000 calls) stays well inside an 8M main thread
stack and still stops an endless recursion before it overflows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/include/debug.hpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/include/debug.hpp b/src/include/debug.hpp
index 95696515..766196b9 100644
--- a/src/include/debug.hpp
+++ b/src/include/debug.hpp
@@ -20,7 +20,9 @@ extern int g_debug_indent_level;
 
 #ifndef DISABLE_DEBUG
 // Note: Set for `curl-sys-0_4_82` build script, which has a log chain of method calls
-# define MAX_INDENT_LEVEL   450
+// - Raised from 450: skim 5.7.3's `#[derive(derive_more::Debug)]` on a 153-field struct is a ~150 call `.field()` chain,
+//   three frames per call. This only guards runaway recursion, real stack use is ~2KiB per call in a chain.
+# define MAX_INDENT_LEVEL   3000
 # define INDENT()    do { g_debug_indent_level += 1; assert(g_debug_indent_level<MAX_INDENT_LEVEL); } while(0)
 # define UNINDENT()    do { g_debug_indent_level -= 1; } while(0)
 # define DEBUG_ENABLED  (debug_enabled() DEBUG_EXTRA_ENABLE)
